        "body": "Part of #256 (owner product acceptance remains open). UoW #301, intent I04 #286.\n\n## What changes\n\nResume and Replay eligibility is decided in one place on the server, exposed and explained, and bound to what the user reviewed.\n\n- **One policy, three consumers.** The engine computes a read-only `RunRecovery` from the run, its pinned definition, initial state and event log. `GET /runs/{id}` returns it as `recovery`, MCP `get_run` returns the same snapshot, and the inspector renders its decisions and text. `POST /runs/{id}/resume` and `/replay` evaluate the same policy again and refuse with the same typed codes (HTTP codes equal the policy codes; refusals are 409, shutdown 503, a missing run 404).\n- **The rules are main's rules, made visible.** Resume continues paused runs and supported failures with the same run ID (a completed failed script, `SCRIPT_EXIT_CODE`, stays resumable); a failed parent owns its identified child's recovery; an uncertain script needs #321's explicit consent; a missing provider session needs #265's fresh-session choice; stop, deadline and unconfirmed-termination failures stay non-resumable. Replay is available at any node the source reached, with a usable definition and state, as on main; the Replay dialog says plainly that the fork runs again from that node as a new run, naming the kinds of work that will run again (scripts, provider turns, child runs, deliveries), and the source's recorded effects and deliveries are never undone or resent.\n- **Observation-bound commands.** Both commands require the `observedSeq` the user reviewed; a stale or repeated intent is refused as `RECOVERY_STALE`. Replay is deduplicated at fork admission: migration `0024_replay_intent` adds the intent's node and observed sequence to the fork row with a uniqueness constraint across the existing indexed `replay_source_run_id` (from #412), so one transaction admits at most one fork per reviewed intent and a lost acknowledgement finds the existing fork. Nothing is appended to a finished run's history.\n- Docs: ADR-0061, docs/05, /07, /09, the run-and-observe and troubleshooting guides, CHANGELOG with the API/MCP upgrade note (`observedSeq` is required), generated references and client.\n\n## Delivery record\n\n- Implementer: the work package's implementer. The orchestrator's review (scan 1 of 3 under D-035) required the eligibility rules to return to main's (the first version had tightened Replay and Resume beyond #256's scope) and Replay deduplication to move from an event on the finished source run to fork admission; both done. Integrated with `main` after #412, #417 and #418 (13 conflicts resolved, migration renumbered to 0024). Record: `docs/qa/2026-10-25-wp-d5-256/REPORT.md`.\n- Gate: an independent audit at the exact head and an independent behaviour QA, then green CI.\n\n## Post-merge human QA (#256)\n\nThe Replay dialog's explanation of repeated work and the inspector's explanations of unavailable actions are product wording the owner should read on a disposable instance.\n\n",
